# The rotation fold's cubins that have mined on a card with every hit verified, one line for each:
#   <toolkit release> <hash>
# The hash is the cubin's sha256 with its string table zeroed (python probes/hand89/asm89.py hash <cubin>).
# probes/hand89/build_rot.py refuses to write pearl_rot_sm89.cubin unless what it built is listed here for the
# toolkit that built it, and the host loads the file beside the core only when its hash is one of these
# (kRotCubins in pearl_host_rot.inc holds the same list). The loop in that file is written by hand, so a new
# line is added only after the file it names has run on an RTX 40 card: probes/verify-hits.js 400 of 400 with
# the fold on, and shares accepted. A line for a loop that is no longer built is taken out: its file may have
# another form of offsets records than this host writes.

# The loop of 12 November 2026: a gather's IADD3 and PRMT late, offsets records of 8 bytes, A's gathers early
# with the scoreboards chosen, a sixth quad (rfold.py al=1 bl=1 bp=1 co=1 ae=1 sbo=7 cq=35).

# CUDA 12.6 (rig01's local toolkit). rig01, RTX 4090: verify-hits 400 of 400 (626 hits, 16 salts), and
# 336.2 and 336.0 TH/s by hashrate.js against 334.6 and 334.7 for the loop before it.
12.6 573b1f133bb216f5853d65e025449b549abf17a9dac27f716c3912be92e2b736

# CUDA 12.8 (what CI builds with, Linux and Windows). The same code as 12.6's, byte for byte; the toolkit's
# version differs, in one byte of the ELF header and one of each kernel's .nv.info section. rig01, RTX 4090:
# verify-hits 400 of 400 (625 hits, 16 salts).
12.8 6e9dfe8ab9eb2396f7835ee03b01ae83641a4c8f43defde8c856cc118525cb8c
